// The format of this file is intended to be directly `include!()` able as a [&'static str] in Rust,
// and a valid python list[str] after stripping the `//` comments at the beginning of lines (from gstreamer.py).
[
// gst-plugins-good
"gstosxaudio",
"gstosxvideo",
// gst-plugins-bad
//
// smb Browser: "gstapplemedia" is deliberately absent, and is not upstreamable
// -- it is a distribution constraint of this product, not a Servo bug.
//
// That plugin's avfvideosrc imports the AVFoundation capture classes
// (AVCaptureDevice, AVCaptureSession, AVCaptureDeviceInput). Mac App Store
// review scans the bundle for those references and reads them as the app
// providing camera functionality, then rejects the submission unless it
// declares com.apple.security.device.camera. smb Browser has no camera feature
// to back that entitlement with: navigator.mediaDevices and getUserMedia are
// both gated on dom_webrtc_enabled, which defaults to false and stays off in
// this build, so web content cannot reach a capture device at all.
//
// The cost is VideoToolbox hardware decode (vtdec) and AudioToolbox atdec.
// gstlibav still decodes H.264 and AAC in software, at higher CPU and energy.
//
// This file is the only place the entry can go. It feeds both mach's dylib
// collection (servo/gstreamer.py) and the runtime plugin list
// (components/servo/gstreamer_plugins.rs), and Servo exits at startup when a
// listed plugin is missing from the bundle -- so deleting only the dylib would
// trade a rejection for a launch crash.
]
